{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-333918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $-4$ and $0.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}=\\,\\,\\frac{1}{2}$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-3+3{e}^{-4t}$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $3-{e}^{-4t}$ |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-333918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & -6{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 2{\\alpha }_{1}t & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-4t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=0,\n$$\n\nboth of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}r(-4t)={e}^{-4t} \\\\ r(0)=1\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}-4t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-4t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{0}=1.\n$$\n\n- Substituting ${\\alpha }_{0}=1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-4t{\\alpha }_{1}+1={e}^{-4t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{4t}({e}^{-4t}-1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-6(-\\frac{1}{4t}({e}^{-4t}-1))t+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{4}({e}^{-4t}-1)+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}({e}^{-4t}-1)+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{-3+3{e}^{-4t}+2}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+3{e}^{-4t}}{2} \\\\ 2{\\alpha }_{1}t & =2(-\\frac{1}{4t}({e}^{-4t}-1))t \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{4}({e}^{-4t}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-4t}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-4t}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1+3{e}^{-4t} & -3+3{e}^{-4t} \\\\ 1-{e}^{-4t} & 3-{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-333918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-333918" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-333918" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1+3e^{-4t}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-333918" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-333918" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-e^{-4t}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-333921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $-2$ and $1.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}=\\,\\,$ |  | $-{e}^{t}+2{e}^{-2t}$ | $-2{e}^{t}+2{e}^{-2t}$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-333921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Explanation:\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & -6{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t & 4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-2t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=t,\n$$\n\nboth of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}r(-2t)={e}^{-2t} \\\\ r(t)={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}-2t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-2t} \\\\ t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtracting the second equation from the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-3t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-2t}-{e}^{t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{3t}({e}^{-2t}-{e}^{t}).\n$$\n\n- Multiplying the second equation by $2$ and adding to the first one, we get\n\n$$\n3{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-2t}+2{e}^{t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{-2t}+2{e}^{t}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\alpha }_{1}t & =3(-\\frac{1}{3t}({e}^{-2t}-{e}^{t}))t \\\\  & =-({e}^{-2t}-{e}^{t}) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =4(-\\frac{1}{3t}({e}^{-2t}-{e}^{t}))t+\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{-2t}+2{e}^{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}((-4{e}^{-2t}+4{e}^{t})+({e}^{-2t}+2{e}^{t})) \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}-{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{t}+2{e}^{-2t} & -2{e}^{t}+2{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{t}-{e}^{-2t} & 2{e}^{t}-{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-333921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-333921" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-333921" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^t-e^{-2t}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-333921" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-333921" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2e^t-e^{-2t}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $0$ and $1.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2-2{e}^{t}$ | $2{e}^{t}-1$ |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & {\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -2{\\alpha }_{1}t & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=0,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=t,\n$$\n\nboth of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}r(0)={e}^{0} \\\\ r(t)={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=1 \\\\ t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the first equation, we immediately get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{0}=1.\n$$\n\n- Substituting ${\\alpha }_{0}=1$ into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt{\\alpha }_{1}+1={e}^{t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{t}({e}^{t}-1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-(\\frac{1}{t}({e}^{t}-1))t+1 \\\\  & =-({e}^{t}-1)+1 \\\\  & =-{e}^{t}+2 \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & =(\\frac{1}{t}({e}^{t}-1))t \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{t}+2 & {e}^{t}-1 \\\\ 2-2{e}^{t} & 2{e}^{t}-1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-334586" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334586" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2-e^t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334586" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334586" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^t-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-323878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $-4$ and $1.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}=\\,\\,\\frac{1}{5}$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-7{e}^{-4t}+7{e}^{t}$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-2{e}^{-4t}+7{e}^{t}$ |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-323878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 7{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -2{\\alpha }_{1}t & 3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-4t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=t,\n$$\n\nboth of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}r(-4t)={e}^{-4t} \\\\ r(t)={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}-4t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-4t} \\\\ t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtraction the second equation from the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-5t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-4t}-{e}^{t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{5t}({e}^{-4t}-{e}^{t}).\n$$\n\n- Multiplying the second equation by $4$ and adding to the first one, we get\n\n$$\n5{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-4t}+4{e}^{t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{-4t}+4{e}^{t}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =6(-\\frac{1}{5t}({e}^{-4t}-{e}^{t}))t+\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{-4t}+4{e}^{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}((-6{e}^{-4t}+6{e}^{t}))+({e}^{-4t}+4{e}^{t})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(7{e}^{-4t}-2{e}^{t}) \\\\ -2{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-2(-\\frac{1}{5t}({e}^{-4t}-{e}^{t}))t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(2{e}^{-4t}-2{e}^{t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}7{e}^{-4t}-2{e}^{t} & -7{e}^{-4t}+7{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-4t}-2{e}^{t} & -2{e}^{-4t}+7{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-323878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-323878" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-323878" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7e^{-4t}-2e^t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-323878" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-323878" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2e^{-4t}-2e^t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $1$ and $4.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}=\\,\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ |  | ${e}^{4t}+2{e}^{t}$ | $2{e}^{4t}-2{e}^{t}$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & 3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=4t,\n$$\n\nboth of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}r(t)={e}^{t} \\\\ r(4t)={e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t} \\\\ 4t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtracting the first equation from the second one, we get\n\n$$\n3t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{4t}-{e}^{t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{3t}({e}^{4t}-{e}^{t}).\n$$\n\n- Multiplying the first equation by $4$ and subtracting the second one, we get\n\n$$\n3{\\alpha }_{0}=4{e}^{t}-{e}^{4t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{1}{3}(4{e}^{t}-{e}^{4t}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =(\\frac{1}{3t}({e}^{4t}-{e}^{t}))t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{4t}-{e}^{t}), \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =3(\\frac{1}{3t}({e}^{4t}-{e}^{t}))t+\\frac{1}{3}(4{e}^{t}-{e}^{4t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}((3{e}^{4t}-3{e}^{t})+(4{e}^{t}-{e}^{4t})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2{e}^{4t}+{e}^{t}),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t}+2{e}^{t} & 2{e}^{4t}-2{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{4t}-{e}^{t} & 2{e}^{4t}+{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-334581" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334581" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{4t}-e^t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334581" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334581" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2e^{4t}+e^t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $1\\pm 4\\text{i}.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)$ | $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 8{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -4{\\alpha }_{1}t & -3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=(1+4\\text{i})t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=(1-4\\text{i})t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((1+4\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(1+4\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(1+4\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & ={e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)) \\\\ ({\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0})+4{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & ={e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\text{i}\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ 4t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{4t}{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{4t}{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\cdot t+{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)) \\\\ -4{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4t}{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-334629" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334629" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\sin(4t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334629" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334629" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\cos(4t)-\\sin(4t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -10 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $2\\pm 5\\text{i}.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{2t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)$ |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -10 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & -10{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t & 7{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=(2+5\\text{i})t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=(2-5\\text{i})t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((2+5\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(2+5\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(2+5\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & ={e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)) \\\\ (2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0})+5{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & ={e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\,{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{5t}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{5t}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\cdot t+{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)+{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\frac{2}{5}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5t}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\cdot t \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-334631" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334631" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\cos(5t)-\\sin(5t)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334631" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334631" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sin(5t)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -13 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $\\pm 5\\text{i}.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\,$ |  | $5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)$ | $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -13 & -1\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -13{\\alpha }_{1}t & -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=5\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-5\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(5\\text{i}t) & ={e}^{5\\text{i}t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}\\cdot 5\\text{i}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+5{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-13{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-13\\cdot \\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =-\\frac{13}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-\\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\cdot t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -13\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-334637" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334637" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-13\\sin(5t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334637" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334637" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\cos(5t)-\\sin(5t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334636" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $\\pm \\text{i}.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}=\\,\\,$ |  | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)$ |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334636" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & {\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -5{\\alpha }_{1}t & -2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\text{i}t) & ={e}^{\\text{i}t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}\\cdot \\text{i}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\frac{1}{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -5{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334636" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-334636" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334636" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sin(t)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334636" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334636" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5\\sin(t)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $-1\\pm 2\\text{i}.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{-t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 4{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -2{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=(-1+2\\text{i})t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=(-1-2\\text{i})t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((-1+2\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(-1+2\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(-1+2\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & ={e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\ (-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0})+2{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & ={e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{2t}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2t}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\cdot t+{e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2t}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\cdot t+{e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-334630" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334630" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\cos(2t)-\\sin(2t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334630" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334630" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\cos(2t)+\\sin(2t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $3,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{3t}\\,\\,$ |  | $1+4t$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $8t$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & -2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 8{\\alpha }_{1}t & -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}r(3t)={e}^{3t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(3t)={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}3t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{3t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n3t{e}^{3t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t}(1-3t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-2{e}^{3t}t \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}(-2t) \\\\ -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-{e}^{3t}t+{e}^{3t}(1-3t) \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}(1-4t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}1+4t & -2t \\\\ 8t & 1-4t\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-334735" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334735" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334735" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334735" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-4t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 12 & -4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $2,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{2t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-3t$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $1-6t$ |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 12 & -4\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & -3{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 12{\\alpha }_{1}t & -4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=2t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}r(2t)={e}^{2t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(2t)={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}2t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{2t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n2t{e}^{2t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}(1-2t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =8{e}^{2t}t+{e}^{2t}(1-2t) \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}(1+6t) \\\\ 12{\\alpha }_{1}t & =12{e}^{2t}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1+6t & -3t \\\\ 12t & 1-6t\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-334733" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334733" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1+6t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334733" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334733" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $1,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-5t$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $1-5t$ |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & -5{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t & -4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}r(t)={e}^{t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(t)={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\nt{e}^{t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t}(1-t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =6{e}^{t}t+{e}^{t}(1-t) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}(1+5t) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t & =5{e}^{t}t \\\\  & ={e}^{t}(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}1+5t & -5t \\\\ 5t & 1-5t\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-334737" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334737" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1+5t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334737" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334737" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $6,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{6t}\\,\\,$ |  | $1+t$ | $t$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & {\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -{\\alpha }_{1}t & 5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=6t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}r(6t)={e}^{6t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(6t)={e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}6t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{6t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{6t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n6t{e}^{6t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{6t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{6t}(1-6t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-{e}^{6t}t \\\\  & ={e}^{6t}(-t), \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =5{e}^{6t}t+{e}^{6t}(1-6t) \\\\  & ={e}^{6t}(1-t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}1+t & t \\\\ -t & 1-t\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-334734" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334734" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334734" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334734" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $1,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | $1-3t$ | $t$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & {\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -9{\\alpha }_{1}t & 4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}r(t)={e}^{t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(t)={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\nt{e}^{t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t}(1-t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-9{e}^{t}t \\\\ 4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =4{e}^{t}t+{e}^{t}(1-t) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}(1+3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}1-3t & t \\\\ -9t & 1+3t\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-334732" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334732" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-9t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334732" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-334732" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1+3t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-335111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-335111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=A\\,{e}^{At}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & =A\\,{e}^{At} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & 8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) \\\\ -8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & -8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-335111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-335111" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" 