in{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-335108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=A\\,{e}^{At}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & =A\\,{e}^{At} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & -5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & -5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/state.json" "file_sha256" "399b2a4cb52da66a546cfbb43cdfdb6df844253a0b0020094008416ff9dfc351"} {"question" "q-335108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058518/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "301f6706f2d15d9c1bc5e5f66232fbd44dd9ad2062d3bd1edaa180642d2c4278"} {"question" "q-335108" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jak